 <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Important Difference on Audit specifically:</strong> do not say "Azure Activity Log = AWS CloudTrail" as a clean 1:1. CloudTrail captures all AWS API calls in one unified event log. Azure splits this across Azure Activity Log (subscription/resource-management-level operations) and Microsoft Entra ID's own sign-in and audit logs (identity and access events) -- you often need both to get the full "who did what" picture CloudTrail gives in one place. GCP's Cloud Audit Logs and OCI Audit are each closer to CloudTrail's single-unified-log model.</p></div>
 <p class="doc-para"><strong>Important Difference on Traces/APM:</strong> AWS's story has two layers -- X-Ray (the original distributed tracing service) and the newer CloudWatch Application Signals (a higher-level APM layer built on top of X-Ray and OpenTelemetry data). Azure's Application Insights is a single, longer-established product covering both roles. GCP splits tracing (Cloud Trace) from error aggregation (Error Reporting) and profiling (Cloud Profiler) as separate but related tools.</p>
