         <div class="doc-section" id="do-not-confuse">
           <div class="doc-section-title">Do Not Confuse These</div>
 <div class="doc-subhead">IAM vs. SSO</div>
-<p class="doc-para">IAM decides <em>what</em> an already-identified entity can do to a resource. SSO is about <em>how a person authenticates once</em> to access multiple systems. Entra ID, IAM Identity Center, Cloud Identity, and OCI Identity Domains handle SSO; AWS IAM, Azure RBAC, Cloud IAM, and OCI IAM policies handle authorization.</p>
+<p class="doc-para">IAM decides <em>what</em> an already-identified entity can do to a resource. SSO is about <em>how a person authenticates once</em> to access multiple systems. Entra ID, IAM Identity Center, Cloud Identity, and OCI Identity Domains handle SSO. AWS IAM, Azure RBAC, Cloud IAM, and OCI IAM policies handle authorization.</p>
 <div class="doc-subhead">Authentication vs. Authorization</div>
 <p class="doc-para">Authentication answers "who are you" (login, MFA). Authorization answers "what are you allowed to do, now that we know who you are." Every IAM system on every provider is fundamentally an authorization system, even though people casually call the whole login experience "IAM."</p>
