strong> Material that still calls this product only "Cloud Functions" is out of date. <strong>Cloud Run functions is the current official name</strong> (Google renamed Cloud Functions and re-platformed it onto Cloud Run infrastructure). Same product line, older name.</li><li><strong>API Gateway vs. Apigee on GCP.</strong> These two get listed as interchangeable alternatives for the same job more often than not. Official Google documentation is clear they are two distinct products for two different scopes: lightweight serverless API fronting versus full enterprise API lifecycle management. Corrected in the DevOps and Application Integration section.</li><li><strong>OCI has no direct Batch or wide-column NoSQL equivalent.</strong> It's tempting to stretch and name some loosely-related OCI feature as the answer for AWS Batch/Azure Batch/Google Cloud Batch, or for AWS Keyspaces/GCP Bigtable. Per this guide's own rule (if there's no reasonable equivalent, say so), both are labeled <strong>No direct equivalent</strong> for OCI instead.</li></ol>
